    "title": "Good Friday: A day of solemn remembrance for Christians",
    "text": "by: Emma McCorkindale Posted: Apr 3, 2026 / 08:22 AM EDT Updated: Apr 3, 2026 / 08:22 AM EDT CHICOPEE, Mass. (WWLP) – It’s Good Friday, a day when Christians mark the day Jesus was crucified. It falls on the Friday before Easter Sunday and is a day of solemn remembrance and reflection on Jesus’s sacrifice for humanity. Traditionally, Good Friday is a day of sorrow, penance, and fasting for many Christians. The National Day Calendar states that the day goes by other names such as Holy Friday, Black Friday, and Great Friday. While Easter has now become a traditional celebration in the secular world, Good Friday has remained a holy and spiritual observance. Will mail, packages be delivered on Good Friday? The United States Postal Service does not list Good Friday nor Easter Sunday as recognized holidays for employees. U.S. Postal Service facilities will have normal operations on Good Friday, meaning USPS facilities will be open for retail transactions and mail will be delivered as usual, USA Today states. UPS pickup and delivery services are available and UPS Store locations will be open on Good Friday. FedEx pickup and delivery services are also available and FedEx Office locations will be open on Friday. Amazon deliveries are generally not affected on Good Friday as it’s not a federal holiday in the U.S. Amazon also does not recognize Easter as a holiday for employees, which mean it will operate as normal. Local News Headlines WWLP-22News, an NBC affiliate, began broadcasting in March 1953 to provide local news, network, syndicated, and local programming to western Massachusetts. Download the 22News Plus app on your TV to watch live-streaming newscasts and video on demand.",
